+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of `document`
+that the pointer refers to. The empty pointer `""` refers to the whole document.
+
+- Throws `SyntaxError` when `pointer` is not a valid JSON Pointer (it must be empty or start with `/`,
+  and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`), and `TypeError` when it is not a string.
+- Throws `RangeError` when the pointer does not resolve: missing member, array index out of range or
+  not a canonical index (`01`, `-1`), the `-` token (it names the element after the last one), or a
+  step into a scalar or `null`.
+- Only own members of objects are resolved, so `/__proto__` or `/constructor` never reach the prototype.
+
+Tests run with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs the TypeScript tests directly).
